# KEAOS Cursor Rules & AI Agent Directives

You are assisting with development on KEAOS (Enterprise Agent Operating Studio).
Read `AGENTS.md` and `src/design.md` for full specifications.

## 1. Design System Rules (src/design.md)
- Geometry: Angular 0px border-radius (`rounded-none`) for all containers, cards, dialogs, inputs, and buttons.
- Full Pill: 9999px border-radius (`rounded-full`) ONLY for status badges and action chips.
- Header: Deep Navy `#001E50` with `#00338D` bottom border.
- Primary CTA: Royal Brand Blue `#00338D` (`hover:bg-[#005EB8]`).
- App Background: Subtle surface gray `#F5F6F8`.
- Card Background: Pure white `#FFFFFF` with `#E0E0E0` border.
- Screens: Use `ScreenScaffold` (`src/components/common/ScreenScaffold.jsx`) and `DESIGN_CLASSES` (`src/constants/designTokens.js`).

## 2. Multi-LLM & Zero-Simulation Mandate
- Never hardcode a single LLM provider.
- Always use `synthesizeMeetingUniversal` and `PROVIDERS` from `src/services/llmService.js`.
- Support Google GenAI, Anthropic Claude, OpenAI GPT-4o, Ollama local, and OpenRouter gateway.
- Ensure fallback to deterministic structured output when API credentials are not provided.

## 3. Strict Anonymity Constraint
- NEVER mention any corporate consulting firm or specific enterprise company name anywhere in code, comments, UI, or docs.
- The platform brand is strictly "KEAOS | Enterprise Agent Operating Studio".

## 4. Socket Enforcement on Visual Canvas
- Sockets are strictly typed: `model-in`, `skill-in`, `mcp-in`, `tools-in`, `gateway-in`, `memory-in`, `policies-in`, `audit-in`, `observability-in`, `cost-benefit-in`.
- Never allow cross-socket connections (e.g. Memory to Model).

## 5. Strict Variable Scoping & Zero-ReferenceError Mandate
- In any node mapping (`nodesWithTheme`, `nodes.map`), ALWAYS initialize all returned data fields (`let connectedModelName = null; let inheritedModelName = null;`) at the top of the outer map iteration scope. Never introduce variables inside an `if (n.type === ...)` block that are referenced in the return object.
- Declare helper callbacks/refs (`takeSnapshot`, `undo`, `redo`) BEFORE any `useEffect` that calls them or lists them in dependencies (No Temporal Dead Zone).

## 6. Strict Browser Origin & Host Invariant (127.0.0.1 Mandate)
- All browser subagents and tools MUST exclusively navigate to `http://127.0.0.1:5173/`.
- NEVER use `http://localhost:5173/`. Browsers isolate localStorage per origin; using 127.0.0.1 ensures the agent sees the exact same storage and state as the user.

## 7. Strict Universal Workflow Execution Invariants (Triple-Mandate)
- **Universal Glowing Visual Parity**: When ANY workflow executes, every triggered node MUST visibly illuminate in real time (Trigger sonar pulse, Pillar discs scale-110 & glow ring, Agent Core ring-4 & spinning brain, Deterministic Box amber glow, Output Node emerald halo, and active dashed wires). Use 250–380ms delays between steps so execution is human-observable.
- **Zero Mandatory File/MP3 Ingestion**: Workflows NEVER require an MP3, audio file, or meeting transcript to execute. Can execute via triggers or direct Execute button.
- **Absolute Zero Presets & Real Data Only**: Never hardcode dummy presets, canned $48,500.00 invoices, fake webhooks, or mock proposal buttons. Always use authentic user inputs or live MCP tools.
- **Drawer Stays Closed**: Hitting Execute must keep the bottom drawer collapsed at 40px so the visual canvas is unobstructed.

## 8. Strict Workflow Preservation, Sandbox Isolation & Locked Workflow Immutability
- **Never Alter Existing Workflows**: Never modify, overwrite, rename, or delete any existing user-created workflow.
- **Diagnostic Isolation via Sandbox Duplication**: When asked to check, diagnose, or experiment by taking control of the browser, ALWAYS create a duplicate copy of the target workflow. Conduct all changes and evaluations strictly in that duplicate. Delete that duplicate when done and satisfied, keeping in the Home tab explicitly only the user's workflows.
- **Locked Workflow Deletion Immunity**: Workflows that are locked (`isLocked` / `isWorkflowLocked`) MUST NEVER be deletable. Protected at both storage engine and UI levels.



